 "standing": "Proposed source and checks complete for root's three checkpoint-3 findings. Source editing STOPPED pending root-review.v4.json. Coauthor technical review; not independent acceptance, not blind acceptance, not user approval, not readiness, not product qualification.",
 "sourceRoot": "/tmp/opensip-design-corrections/bv4-corrections-author.v3/work",
 "dispositions": [
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-DEFAULT-PUBLIC-CARRIER/required-projection-regression",
   "position": "AGREE - this was a regression I introduced, and the most serious of the three",
   "whatIDid": "I added `if k in envelope['parity']` to render so an old fixture would keep passing. That silently weakened the inherited required-field behavior for EVERY declared parity field, not just the new one: a missing required-coverage simply vanished from all five formats instead of failing. Section 8 already says a missing declared field is a required-delivery operational fault, never a successful partial rendering.",
   "correction": "strict access restored - `{k: envelope['parity'][k] for k in command['parityFields']}` - with the reason recorded in the code so it is not re-weakened. Callers with no selection supply the explicit empty collection {stepCount:0,totalNoticeCount:0,steps:[]} rather than omitting the field. The existing conversion stands: the host maps the projection exception to operational-failed / DELIVERY.REQUIRED_FAILED with faultCause delivery-required, retaining a committed RunId; the helper exception alone is not a public termination, which section 8 states explicitly.",
   "verified": [
    "a-missing-declared-parity-field-is-never-silently-omitted.{capability-availability,required-coverage,verdict}",
    "the-strict-projection-covers-the-inherited-fields-not-only-the-new-one (repair-verify net-new-findings)",
    "a-complete-projection-still-renders-in-every-format",
    "an-invocation-that-selected-nothing-supplies-the-explicit-empty-collection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-DEFAULT-PUBLIC-CARRIER/analysis-command-completeness",
   "position": "AGREE - confirmed",
   "correction": "capability-availability is now declared by EVERY requestClass=analysis command - the fifth, repair-verify, was the omission - and a drift control asserts the set of commands declaring it is exactly the set of analysis commands, so neither a new analysis command nor a non-analysis command can drift.",
   "verified": [
    "every-analysis-command-declares-capability-availability-as-a-parity-field (5 of 5)",
    "no-non-analysis-command-silently-acquires-the-field",
    "the-declared-parity-field-reaches-every-applicable-renderer-of-every-analysis-command"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-PUBLICATION/current-contract-reconciliation",
   "position": "AGREE - all four confirmed",
   "corrections": [
    "native 1.4's opening sentence published the superseded flat {noticeCount,notices[]}; it now names the per-step CapabilityAvailabilityStepV1 and the composed {stepCount,totalNoticeCount,steps[]}, and identifies the leaf step projection versus the enclosing invocation. Workflows 8's introductory sentence is corrected the same way.",
    "native 1.4's authority limits discussed truncating defects/defectsFound although doctor is no longer this carrier and the collection cannot truncate; they now state the actual bounds. release_absence_notices' docstring no longer calls itself the only candidate-only route and records that it returns ONE step's account.",
    "native 10's aliases paragraph claimed `No public DomainDetailCode is added` while the same section adds four; it now states four are added, named and justified, and that no D9 class, exit code, reason code or error code changes.",
    "the elision prose promised a retained raw diagnostic without naming a carrier. It now confines the guarantee to what is PUBLISHED - the bounded subject and its digest - names no store, states the exact deterministic encoding normatively (UTF-8 composed subject, 1024 bound, marker `...#sha256:`, lowercase hex SHA-256, exactly 1024 characters) and uses the ordinary collision-resistance assumption instead of a literal impossibility claim."
   ],
   "verified": [
    "the-elision-encoding-is-exactly-as-published",
    "the full suite re-run after every prose change"
   ]
  }
 ],
